<http://data.silknow.org/object/6959cbf4-c3be-3c70-9efb-e9e37d135080>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "A parasol with handle of composition ivory carved with lily-of-the-valley design and canopy of Brussels bobbin lace applied to machine-made net, over black silk taffeta. Lined with white silk taffeta and trimmied with black satin ribbon raced with white satin."@en , "The parasol was a popular accessory during the 19th century, a period before the sun-tanned face became fashionable.  Many parasols were made of lace, and like this example, lined with a contrasting silk to show off the design of the lace and enhance its sun-shading properties.    The handle is made of elephant tusk ivory."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/0d67d0b4-12fd-3961-9afa-71f1ea047e5d> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/0fd1d9c8-aa2a-3ea4-b5ac-7274f916d508> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "The parasol was a popular accessory during the 19th century, a period before the sun-tanned face became fashionable.  Many parasols were made of lace, and like this example, lined with a contrasting silk to show off the design of the lace and enhance its sun-shading properties.    The handle is made of elephant tusk ivory."@en , "A parasol with handle of composition ivory carved with lily-of-the-valley design and canopy of Brussels bobbin lace applied to machine-made net, over black silk taffeta. Lined with white silk taffeta and trimmied with black satin ribbon raced with white satin."@en ;
